## Why This Is Asked
New angle: third-party feed integrity across regions; captures data lineage and external fault containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with lineage; - region-aware lifecycle; - logs/traces integration; - metrics for containment; - RCA and canary plan.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model outline
type CAPA = {
  id: string; region: string; feedId: string; version: string;
  evidenceUris: string[]; logTraceIds: string[]; t_incident: string; t_detected: string;
  containmentStatus: 'Identified'|'Contained'|'Investigated'|'Remediated'|'Verified'|'Closed';
  recurrenceRate?: number; mttr?: number;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you simulate data-feed corruption to validate the canary rollout?
- What tamper-evident mechanisms would you add to the evidence store?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical CAPA design skills: data modeling, lifecycle governance, lightweight APIs, and measurable containment strategies in a multi-tenant, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model tailored to tenants/regions
- Lifecycle state machine with auditable transitions
- Minimal REST API for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region/tenant-aware metrics to prove containment
- RCA template and canary remediation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  tenants: string[];
  regions: string[];
  evidence: string[];
  batchInfo: {
    schedule: string;
    duration: number;
    resources: string[];
  };
  rootCause: string;
  corrective: string;
  preventive: string;
  owner: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
};

// Lifecycle states
type CAPAState = 'Identified' | 'Contained' | 'Investigating' | 'Corrected' | 'Verified';

// REST API endpoints
POST /capas
PUT /capas/:id
GET /capas?tenant=:t&region=:r&state=:s
```

## Metrics & Containment
- Tenant/region latency percentiles pre/post containment
- Batch job resource utilization by tenant/region
- Error rates and success rates during remediation
- Canary deployment success metrics by region

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around operational risk in alert routing, including change control, cross-tenant impact, and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model (evidence, lineage, owners)
- Lifecycle with detect/contain/remediate/verify and SLAs
- Canary-based rollback and change control
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, MTTR

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express-like minimal CAPA create endpoint (illustrative)
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const capa = req.body;
  // persist CAPA with evidence, lineage, owners
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', ...capa });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollback plan for alert-rule changes?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate containment and prevent recurrence?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a data-path incident into a systematic CAPA plan, from data model to evidence mgmt and preventive action. Evaluates clarity, traceability, and practical canary-based rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model
- State machine
- Evidence management and RCA
- Region-aware metrics
- Canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
